asm 0xac9e..0xad01 (re_out/fist_dat_image.bin): SS=DS=DGROUP=0x1c00; DI=param_1 = object near-offset;
SI/BX derived near-offsets; every N(reg) = word/dword[DGROUP:off].  Ghidra deref'd the near-offsets as
HOST pointers (piVar1=*roster-entry, piVar4, *param_1@+0x40) and int*-scaled the WORD/DWORD reads
(piVar1[0x17] vs asm +0x2e; *(long*)(piVar1+2)/(+4) vs asm +4/+8).  di+0x40 = WORD (testw/orw), not uint.
Rebased all to g_mem+0x1c000+near-offset with asm-exact widths + the si-chain [0x9796]->[+4]->[*2-0x67d0]
+byte[di+0x1c]*4 and bx=word[(byte[di+0x1b]<<3)+0x6d3c].  03a9 is a fixed-point rotate (05e2/05dd) whose
param_3 is unused, so bx (near-offset) passes through safely.  Only reached via 22dd's cursor-bracket
(patch 395) on the SYRIA2/4 CYPRUS4 AZER3 UKRAINE1 path; no passing flow reaches it (the old host-ptr
deref would have crashed them) -> regression-safe.

